-## Release 1.10.0 (candidate 1.10.0rc5, not a final release): a request set aside and asked again (C1)
+## Release 1.10.0 (candidate 1.10.0rc6, not a final release): a request set aside and asked again (C1)
+
+**1.10.0rc6: three defects found by the full run F2 (1.10.0rc5, 2026-11-16) corrected, and the run's order
+and product pages chosen from F2's traces.** Each defect has a focused test that fails on 1.10.0rc5 and
+passes here.
+
+* **OR-19, a re-ask answered before its products loaded.** F2 stopped (`STORE_NOT_VERIFIED`, exit 7, not
+  resumable) on a re-ask of Espresso Coffee page 2 whose own search named the configured store (53100502,
+  PICKUP) while its page state carried no product's data and its grid drew 3 cards. Such an answer now counts
+  no product, keeps its identity and the request's original reason, and is asked again within the task's
+  bounded retries or set aside; an unresolved repeat or spent retries leave the listing incomplete. Another
+  store, another fulfillment or a page without its store proof still stop the run.
+* **OR-20, `validate-export` within a small VM's memory.** The command held every page's text and every
+  embedded product at once and was killed on F2's 575 pages. It now reads one stored page at a time and keeps
+  only the distinct price statements it needs; it checks every record against them, every capture named by
+  the supporting log against its stored bytes and hash (missing, corrupted, unreadable, not named), and lists
+  each mismatch with the record's and the source's values. The report states the seconds, the sources read
+  and the peak memory.
+* **OR-04, the Coupons row read only when its list loaded.** Seven of twelve earlier answers rendered the
+  coupons tab before its list loaded and were recorded as read with 0 coupons. The page is now read as
+  loaded with cards, loaded and empty (a stated 0 without the loading indicator) or not loaded; a page not
+  loaded is asked again after the listings (at most `coupons_attempts`, 4, `coupons_retry_wait_s`, 60 s,
+  apart, across restarts). A run whose plan names the row is complete only when it is READ (G3; the dataset
+  label; the coverage file's row 0; the manifest's `routes`). A product page still loading proves no coupon
+  absent (`unread_loading`).
+* **Order.** A listing read through its subdivisions is finished before the plan's next listing starts
+  (F2 left 25 listings above the window with none of their subdivisions read). `run --rows-first 22,27,15`
+  reads those rows first, the others after in the CSV's order (recorded as the run's order; not a scope
+  limit).
+* **Product pages.** `run --term-upc UPC` (repeatable) reads the own pages of the named products only, once
+  per run when their cards are met; with `coverage.read_product_terms` on, every tile's page would be one
+  more request.
+
+### C1 and the earlier candidates of 1.10.0
+
 
 On 2026-11-09 some answers to a listing's page N listed page 1's products, and some first pages of a
 listing above the site's 250-result window named no child listing and no brand to subdivide it by; minutes
